Nutrient Control Design Manual — US EPA (@wu-nutrients-epa: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_5MZ6AJ5ZW61R793FSA311WAJ2G
US EPA, EPA/600/R-10/100, August 2010. Prepared by the Cadmus Group for the agency. [Official full text](https://nepis.epa.gov/Exe/ZyPURL.cgi?Dockey=P1008KTD.TXT) · [Official PDF](https://www.epa.gov/sites/production/files/2019-02/documents/nutrient-control-design-manual.pdf).

Read the complete technical argument progressively. Chapters 3–5 establish chemical phosphorus removal and biological nitrogen/phosphorus transformations; chapters 6–8 connect configurations, objectives and process selection; chapters 9–10 develop design and modelling. Reconstruct an example before judging a simulated upgrade. Use the references to locate the underlying measurements and competing models.

The official text, contents and selected stoichiometric and design sections were inspected on 30 October 2026. This is a 2010 technical reference, not a statement of current discharge law. Public access does not erase contractor or third-party notices; retain the selected document's credits. Its US regulatory context needs the current requirements of the actual jurisdiction.

